o try and link two independent clauses . While the comma is, as we said, a versatile piece of punctuation, it is not str
ong enough to link two independent clauses. If you want to use it in this way, you must use a conjunction (a linking wor
d) alongside it. The changes were made, and the results were recorded. If you want to use a conjunction with a comma in 
this way, then you use a very specific conjunction known as a ‘coordinating conjunction’. These are conjunctions whi
